ce  when hizdar offers daenerys some food  belwas eats it instead  and he later becomes very ill but  because he's such a large man he does  survive  although it does have a major effect on  his strength and weight  now i will say he's not necessarily a  very fascinating character but he's  still one that i would have liked to  have seen nonetheless  the next character on my list is the  famous fool known as patchface  i think he's one of the most interesting  and mysterious characters  in a song of ice and fire we don't know  what his real name is but the reason why  he's referred to as patchface is because  of the tattoos on his face  and head he has these markings on his  face because  this is the fashion in the free city of  atlantis for slaves who serve as jesters  how this character ends up in the  service of stannis baratheon  is kind of interesting he was bought by  stannis father stephen baratheon  who was sent over to the free cities by  the mad king in search of a bride for  his son rhaegar targaryen  he never does find a suitable bride for  rhaegar but when stephon baratheon  discovers patchface  he immediately sends a letter back to  his maester at storm's end  in the letter he wrote we have found the  most splendid fool  he's only a boy yet he's nimble as a  monkey  and extremely witty he juggles and  riddles  and even does magic he could also sing  songs in four different languages  we've bought his freedom and we hope to  bring him back home with us  robert will be delighted with him and  maybe he will even show stannis how to  laugh  unfortunately however he would never see  his sons again  robert and stannis watched as their  father's ship was smashed against the  rocks and swallowed by the waters that  were within sight of storm's end  everyone on their father's ship died  well  everyone except for good old patchface  the days after the ship  sank his lifeless naked body washed up  on the shore  the maester thought he was dead but when  someone gr