ng for catelyn's daughters  in hopes of getting them back home safe  lady stoneheart doesn't believe her  though  so she gave brienne a choice either you  and your friends hang  or you bring me jaime lannister at first  brienne was willing to give her life  before handing her jamie  but at the very last moment right before  she lost consciousness  she did agree to find him and bring him  back to lady stoneheart  and the brotherhood without banners the  books more or less  end shortly after brienne finds jaime  she did convince him to help her save  sansa stark from the hound now what's  really interesting is  brienne convinces jaime to go with her  alone or else she says the hound will  kill sansa  this is one of the storylines i'm  looking forward to reading the most  in the winds of winter i really wish  they would have went in this direction  in the show  i think it's far more interesting than  some of the other things they did with  these characters  but maybe that's just me another  character i wish we would have seen in  game of thrones was victarion greyjoy  the brother of euron and balon greyjoy  victarion is a very large man who is  known for being a fierce warrior in  battle  now you might not know this if you have  only seen the show  but the reason why euron greyjoy was  gone for so long was because he was  exiled  by his brother baelon you see euron not  only seduced victarion's wife  but he also got her with child when  victarion found out what happened  he beat his wife to death victarion  would have even done the same  thing to euron but he did not want to be  known as a kinslayer  that's why baylon sent him away  victarion has never married since  and he has never forgiven euron either  now  as soon as geron wins the king's moon is  where things begin to get really  interesting with the greyjoy brothers  this is when euron demands that  victarion sail across the narrow sea  and offer a proposal of marriage to none  other than the mother of dragons  